wasm32-wasip1 has no positional read: olean_fs::pread exists for unix and windows only

Upstream added olean_fs.rs (the .olean reader's file access) with a `pread` helper
under #[cfg(unix)] / #[cfg(windows)]; on wasm32-wasip1 neither applies and the crate
does not compile. std::os::wasi::fs::FileExt is unstable, so the wasi branch seeks and
reads through &File (every read names its offset, nothing relies on the cursor).
The ndjson harness never opens .olean files; this only makes the crate build.
Upstream: none (wasm32 is not an upstream target; checked 2026-11-24).

diff --git a/crates/con-ron/src/olean_fs.rs b/crates/con-ron/src/olean_fs.rs
index 1aa8ba3..2bcde0b 100644
--- a/crates/con-ron/src/olean_fs.rs
+++ b/crates/con-ron/src/olean_fs.rs
@@ -100,6 +100,15 @@ fn pread(f: &std::fs::File, buf: &mut [u8], off: u64) -> std::io::Result<usize>
     f.seek_read(buf, off)
 }
 
+/// wasm32-wasip1: `std::os::wasi::fs::FileExt` is unstable, so seek and read
+/// through `&File` (the handle's cursor moves; every read here names its offset).
+#[cfg(target_os = "wasi")]
+fn pread(mut f: &std::fs::File, buf: &mut [u8], off: u64) -> std::io::Result<usize> {
+    use std::io::{Read, Seek, SeekFrom};
+    f.seek(SeekFrom::Start(off))?;
+    f.read(buf)
+}
+
